# Architect orchestration trigger

When **any** of the conditions below match the user message, you MUST read and follow `.cursor/rules/architect.mdc` end-to-end (plan, Task dispatch per step, validate, deliver, @Memory-Manager last). Do not stop after publishing the plan unless the user explicitly asked for plan-only.

## Activation conditions (any one is enough)

- User mentions `@Architect`
- User asks to **orchestrate**, run the **full flow**, **coordinate agents**, or **deliver the result** (not just analyze)
- User describes work across **multiple layers**, projects, or specialist domains (backend + UI, DB + API, Docker + app, tests + feature, security + auth, etc.)
- User uses phrases like: *full flow*, *end to end*, *execute the plan*, *deliver it done*, *multi-agent* (Spanish equivalents also count: *flujo completo*, *de punta a punta*, *entrégamelo hecho*)

## Template kit work (prefer @Template-Architect)

When the user only wants to **install**, **upgrade**, or **extend** **AOK** (Agent Orchestration Kit: profiles, `install.sh`, new `.mdc` in the kit), follow `.cursor/rules/template-architect.mdc` instead of forcing the full @Architect loop — unless they also asked for application implementation in the same request.

## Exclusions (do NOT force full orchestration)

- User explicitly says: *plan only*, *analyze only*, *don't implement* (Spanish: *solo plan*, *solo analiza*, *no ejecutes*)
- Pure questions, definitions, or read-only explanations with no implementation request
- Single trivial change in one file with one clear action
- **Kit / docs-only work:** request touches only `docs/`, `template/`, `profiles/`, `scripts/`, or `.github/` — use @Template-Architect or direct edit, not full app orchestration
- **`--no-suggest-layers` / validate-only** shell tasks on the template repo itself

## On activation

1. Adopt the @Architect role for this thread.
2. Execute the orchestration loop in `architect.mdc`.
3. Load `.cursor/skills/architect-orchestration/SKILL.md` for Phase 1–4 templates.
4. For standard features, prefer `scripts/run-workflow.sh .architecture/workflows/feature-delivery.yaml --prompt "<request>"` to seed the plan.
5. Final message MUST use **Phase 4** (Section A + B + participation bars), not only the execution plan.